{"text": " 250 million, that's how much my business has made in total last year. But before that, here's every single business I tried before winning. Number one, the free training project. So I actually started a non-profit where I would just give away fitness services in exchange for people donating money to a charity. From there, I shifted that into a for-profit thing for only my 20 best friends called Skinny the Swole from the guys I was in the fraternity with. From there, I didn't wanna keep doing that because I wanted to be legit, so I started a brick and mortar gym called Transformation Center that eventually became United Fitness. That was brick and mortar. I scaled that to six locations. While I was going on with that, I thought maybe I should start also a chiropractor agency because I was pretty good at marketing and sales. And then I thought, you know what, why have two businesses when you could have three? And I started a dental marketing agency. And then I thought, hey, why have three businesses when you could have four? So then I started a gym turnaround business where I would fly around from gym and I would actually do gym launches where I'd fill the gym up in 30 days, then started scaling that out. Obviously, Layla, smarter than me, was like, hey, what if we did the one thing that actually makes us money, which is launching gyms? So I shut down the other two businesses, even though I had different partners in all of them, and even though I was the CEO slash Rainmaker in all of them, I shut all of those down and went all in on gym launch. I kept doing that, but then all of a sudden that stopped working as well. And so then we had the brilliant idea, hey, Layla, you lost 100 pounds. Why don't we start Queen Transformation? We'll just sell directly to people online, the way I had actually started this business four or five years earlier, and we started doing that. And so within a few days of absolute caffeine and stimulant up to my eyeballs, I wrote the best sales letter of my life, started ring ads to it, and we started making money. We scaled that for five years. And then in that process, we also started our supplement company, Prestige Labs, the third year in the business. And the fourth year, we started Allen, which is a lead working software. We sold all three of those companies in 2021, $46.2 million. From there, we started acquisition.com with the 40 plus million in distributions and the $46 million sale. We took the cash and started investing in companies. And today, five years later, our aggregate portfolio is $250 million a year. The business that you're in right now is probably not the one you're gonna end up in, but the lessons you learn are the ones that you'll keep.", "segments": [{"id": 0, "seek": 0, "start": 0.0, "end": 2.34, "text": " 250 million, that's how much my business", "tokens": [50364, 11650, 2459, 11, 300, 311, 577, 709, 452, 1606, 50481], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09542670033194801, "compression_ratio": 1.7284595300261096, "no_speech_prob": 0.006301932968199253}, {"id": 1, "seek": 0, "start": 2.34, "end": 3.86, "text": " has made in total last year.", "tokens": [50481, 575, 1027, 294, 3217, 1036, 1064, 13, 50557], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09542670033194801, "compression_ratio": 1.7284595300261096, "no_speech_prob": 0.006301932968199253}, {"id": 2, "seek": 0, "start": 3.86, "end": 5.94, "text": " But before that, here's every single business", "tokens": [50557, 583, 949, 300, 11, 510, 311, 633, 2167, 1606, 50661], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09542670033194801, "compression_ratio": 1.7284595300261096, "no_speech_prob": 0.006301932968199253}, {"id": 3, "seek": 0, "start": 5.94, "end": 7.34, "text": " I tried before winning.", "tokens": [50661, 286, 3031, 949, 8224, 13, 50731], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09542670033194801, "compression_ratio": 1.7284595300261096, "no_speech_prob": 0.006301932968199253}, {"id": 4, "seek": 0, "start": 7.34, "end":